course: dictionary
lesson: 6230
title: Memory tricks
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mnemonic is a trick that helps your memory. You might know it as a rhyme, a saying, or a word made from the first letters of other words. «Richard Of York Gave Battle In Vain» is a mnemonic for the colours of the rainbow, because the first letters match red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet.
explain: Mnemonics are useful when something is hard to remember, but a rule would be tricky to learn. «Big Elephants Can Always Understand Small Elephants» helps you spell «because», which breaks the usual spelling rules. Rules still help with most other words.
explain: You will meet mnemonics in maths and science too. «BIDMAS» (or «PEMDAS») reminds you of the order to do calculations in. «Never Eat Shredded Wheat» helps you remember the compass points: north, east, south and west.
explain: Ask yourself: is this a rule that works for most words, or a trick for a few very hard ones? If it is hard to remember, make up your own mnemonic. Say it out loud, and it will stick.
fact: A mnemonic is a memory trick.
fact: Mnemonic can also be an adjective, meaning helping the memory.
fact: A mnemonic can be a rhyme, a saying, or a word made from first letters.
fact: «Richard Of York Gave Battle In Vain» helps you remember the rainbow colours.
fact: «Big Elephants Can Always Understand Small Elephants» helps you spell «because».
fact: Mnemonics work best for a few very hard words; rules help with most others.
exercise: What is a mnemonic? | A long word that is hard to say | A type of maths sum | *A trick that helps you remember something
exercise: «Big Elephants Can Always Understand Small Elephants» helps you spell which word? | *because | elephant | small | understand
exercise: Which mnemonic helps you remember the compass points? | Richard Of York Gave Battle In Vain | Big Elephants Can Always Understand Small Elephants | BIDMAS | *Never Eat Shredded Wheat
test: What does mnemonic mean when it is used as an adjective? | Very old | Dangerous to walk on | *Helping the memory
test: «Richard Of York Gave Battle In Vain» is a mnemonic for what? | *The colours of the rainbow | The compass points | The order of operations in maths | The spelling of because
exam: Which statement is true? | A mnemonic is only used in science lessons | A mnemonic is a long sentence with no purpose | *A mnemonic is a memory trick that helps with a few very hard words | A mnemonic is a rule that works for every single word
